00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.200
So if I have multiple
frequencies--

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.140
let's look at the simplest--

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:26.830
if I just have two
frequencies, what happens?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:31.640
Let's say one frequency is
omega 0 plus delta omega.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:36.790
And correspondingly, I
have k0 plus delta k,

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.240
because it's not linear.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:43.480
So I have omega 0 minus delta
omega and k0 minus delta k.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:47.770
So those are two different
waves with slightly different--

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:55.180
they all centralize to omega 0,
but they are small spreading,

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:58.910
delta omega delta k.

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:00.100
And now I have--

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:03.070
really what's propagating
this simultaneously two

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:07.120
waves I generated and the
superposition of these two

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.820
waves.

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:14.140
So if I look at the
superimposed wave, a--

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:16.300
I'm assuming they are
same amplitude just

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:18.730
to make life simpler--

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:24.220
and a minus i omega
0 plus delta omega

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:36.190
t minus k plus the delta kx k0
and plus the other frequency

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:42.610
and the wave vector is minus
i omega 0 minus delta omega

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:49.990
t minus k0 minus delta k x.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:56.350
And I have the superposition
of this real signal that

00:19:56.350 --> 00:20:01.880
propagated in the media because
it has two waves in the signal.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:06.340
And when I add this up, you
have a central frequency omega

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.500
k0 I can pull out.

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:14.360
Then I have a plus term, a
minus term in the exponent.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:18.040
So you do your
algebra, what you get

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:28.480
is a 2a cosine delta omega times
t delta k times x, and then

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:34.060
exponential minus i
omega 0t minus k0 x.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.950
So this is the
result of when I have

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:48.010
two waves with a small
separation in frequency

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:51.340
and wave vector.

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:56.350
And you look at this
now what's propagating,

00:20:56.350 --> 00:21:04.510
here I have a high frequency
omega 0 k0 central one.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:13.060
Here I have not a cosine that
modulates this frequency.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:16.510
So what I really have is
a cosine signal that's

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:21.550
delta omega delta k, so
which is slower, typically.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.730
And then this is the
amplitude of the--

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:34.330
so at the center, I have
omega 0 k0 modulated.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:38.725
So this is the FM signal.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:46.020
Is it AM or FM?

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:46.830
AM signal.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:51.090
You're modulating the amplitude
of the central frequency,

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:52.320
right?

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:59.430
So now I have the
outer envelope, which

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:02.160
is cosine omega t minus kx.

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:04.590
Now if you think
about what energy--

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.810
say the pointing vector.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:10.230
For example, when I think
about electromagnetic wave,

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:16.650
my pointing vector is E
cross H. And of course I

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:20.820
have one half real part of that.

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:28.740
Now if I have this term inside
equals H, E has this term.

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.910
H complex conjugate also has
this term, but as a plus.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:39.190
That this term actually drop
out when you do equals H.

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:42.090
So what it is really,
then, the energy

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:43.800
is actually the front term here.

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:51.240
So what energies are propagated
is like, in this case,

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:54.150
it's a slower
packet propagating.

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:57.050
That's a wave packet.

00:22:57.050 --> 00:22:59.420
And the speed of this
propagation-- now

00:22:59.420 --> 00:23:04.010
if I look at this
factor there, is dx dt.

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:14.750
So the dx dt is
delta omega delta k.

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:20.170
So this is actually whether the
propagation-- this wave packet

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:23.420
