00:27:42.500 --> 00:27:46.580
But say most time, this
is 0 and velocity is 0.

00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:50.210
So if you think about it the
parabolic bend, the group

00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:52.790
velocity--

00:27:52.790 --> 00:27:57.590
let's say here kx is d omega.

00:27:57.590 --> 00:28:05.360
Omega is E over h bar, right,
that's omega, and d kx,

00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:09.070
let's say in the x direction.

00:28:09.070 --> 00:28:15.300
And E, if it's a parabolic
bend, then you can say

00:28:15.300 --> 00:28:18.960
is h bar kx over m.

00:28:18.960 --> 00:28:21.360
So this is P over
m, momentum divided

00:28:21.360 --> 00:28:26.100
by mass, that's consistent when
we have in the classical limit.

00:28:30.870 --> 00:28:33.150
But on the other
hand, if you say OK,

00:28:33.150 --> 00:28:41.780
my E equals h bar squared
k squared over 2m,

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:43.530
so this is a team for
our parabolic event.

00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:54.610
And if I just use the phrase
velocity all for this,

00:28:54.610 --> 00:28:59.140
I will not gather the
same as group velocity.

00:28:59.140 --> 00:29:02.625
So group velocity is like my
